     ExpressionUUID->"cc7cccf3-906e-4170-8114-c7b5b21545db"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "88b87d12-825e-468a-9f9c-14acbf0dc0d0"], Cell[
    "Fixed", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "da71167d-d834-40fc-b176-6072e1892b70"], Cell["\<\
lock the current branch as the starting point for later steps\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e7db3c41-3809-40d5-9726-293df6a4f46a"]}
  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"492e9727-eb4b-4ac5-b774-\
5ca39b8703b2"],

Cell["\<\
Branch and Diffuse are the two ways to look at a family. Diffuse draws every \
realisation at once, with intensity following multiplicity, which is the \
right view for seeing where an object is concentrated. Branch picks one, \
which is the right view for following a single construction through to the \
end.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"87b483d9-e859-4dd9-ad2a-369396e6ffa9"],

Cell["\<\
Fixed matters on long constructions. Without it, each step re-solves against \
every branch of the previous ones and the instance count multiplies. Fixing a \
branch collapses that.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"daa27f82-5f75-4f37-a8a3-16b6af2f8de5"],

